# Data and runs

- Types in `battery_fleet/` are the law. No column the types don’t know.
- A run is a folder with `run.db`. The card lives in that database.
- Start a run only with `python -m battery_fleet run scenarios/…`. Do not `mkdir` a run. Do not edit `runs/index.json`. The index is a scan.
- Location ≠ unit. Load and island sit on the location. Ticks sit on the unit.
- Local policy always runs. HQ is a privilege when the location is linked. No last-HQ-setpoint.
- Do not bake “only one run,” “always online,” or “home = battery.”
- If a file in this package goes over ~250 lines, split it.
